 "response": "Getosti's budget is **$2095K**.\n\n**Which records count.** Only Finance Office budget entries change the budget. Messages from other teams, and Finance notes such as cost-centre codes or audit scheduling, have no effect.\n\n**How withdrawals were handled.** Each withdrawal was followed back along its chain. The last withdrawal that is not itself withdrawn decides whether the original update counts. Some decisive chains:\n\n- **#0002 (+$472K) counts.** #0161 withdraws #0081. That revives #0032, which cancels #0015. That revives #0009, which cancels #0007. So #0002 stands.\n- **#0003 (+$547K) is out.** #1164 cancels #0154. That revives #0021, which cancels #0013. That revives #0012, which withdraws #0003.\n- **#0006, #0020, #0022 and #0029 are out.** Their chains end in withdrawals that stay in effect.\n- **#0028, #0051, #0052, #0071, #0177, #0201, #0236, #0414 and #0420 count.** In each chain, the withdrawal against them was itself withdrawn.\n- **#0206, #0339, #0384, #0533 and #0568 are out.** The final effective withdrawal in each chain removes them.\n\n**Calculation.** Starting from the $1730K set in #0001, I applied every remaining increase and decrease once, in record order. The running total ends at $2095K after #1590.\n\nANSWER: $2095K",
